  "reason": "Evidence: The best-performing configuration so far is config_010 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.7062). Clear trends show weighted fusion > concat, imagenet_vit_l > resnet50, and scvi_n200 > pca_n2000. The one untested dimension within this strong setting is the aggregation method: all top configs use avgpool, but transformer aggregation could better model inter-profile relationships in the multiprofile setting. Question: Does upgrading aggregation from avgpool to transformer, while keeping the proven scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + weighted backbone, push accuracy above 0.706? Why this is the best next experiment: config_020 is a single-variable extension of the current best, directly testing whether the multiprofile aggregation bottleneck limits performance. It avoids the very high cost of PCA-based configs (config_003 cost 36.42 GPU hrs) while leveraging the cheap scvi_n200 encoder. Expected relative cost is moderate—slightly higher than config_010 (4.82 GPU hrs) due to the transformer aggregation layer, likely in the range of 8–15 GPU hours, making it a cost-effective high-information experiment with 5 experiments remaining in budget."
